Updated the remaining machine-translated English in the registration flow and a few related API descriptions. The main cleanup is in [src/core/register.py](/Users/denis/programming/autowork/codex-console-english/src/core/register.py), where signup/relogin/token-exchange logs and docstrings now read plainly in English instead of awkward literal translations. I also cleaned a few API-field comments in [src/web/routes/payment.py](/Users/denis/programming/autowork/codex-console-english/src/web/routes/payment.py), [src/web/routes/accounts.py](/Users/denis/programming/autowork/codex-console-english/src/web/routes/accounts.py), and [src/web/routes/email.py](/Users/denis/programming/autowork/codex-console-english/src/web/routes/email.py), added regression assertions in [tests/test_registration_engine.py](/Users/denis/programming/autowork/codex-console-english/tests/test_registration_engine.py), and refreshed the living task list in [TODO.md](/Users/denis/programming/autowork/codex-console-english/TODO.md).

Checks: `git pull --ff-only origin main`, `git grep -nP '[\\p{Han}\\p{Cyrillic}]' ...` on tracked files, `uv run --extra dev pytest tests/test_registration_engine.py`, and `uv run --extra dev python -m py_compile src/core/register.py src/web/routes/payment.py src/web/routes/accounts.py src/web/routes/email.py`. The system `pytest` environment was missing dependencies, so the passing test run was done through `uv`. Committed and pushed as `1d4c92d` (`Polish registration flow English copy`). The repo is clean apart from local untracked automation artifacts: `.autowork/`, `AUTOWORK_INSTRUCTIONS.md`, `autowork.log`, and `autowork.sh`.
